DESCRIPTION:Every artifact has a story\, and sometimes the story is so cree
 py\, weird\, or fascinating it becomes lore. Explore the history of some o
 f the strangest and most bizarre objects in UNT Special Collections  in Th
 e Legend of Eppy and Other Artifacts of Lore. This is one “lore drop” 
 you won’t want to miss.\n\n \n\nLike the apocalyptic paintings made by a
  Sunday school teacher in Denton to scare kids straight\, or the tiny skul
 l kept by a boy who loved his pet hamster\, Mildred\, so much he could nev
 er say goodbye. This exhibit explores the concept of lore through the arti
 facts we leave behind\, like photographs of the infamous “Wyooter” cry
 ptid\, and a book so small it caused the typesetter to go blind.\n\n \n\nN
 o artifact in Special Collections has such an inspired lore as Eppy\, an i
 nfamous former mascot that was lost\, found\, stolen and returned with a s
 uspicious injury. Countless Reddit threads document student’s search for
  Eppy. Abandoned after his retirement in the mid-1990’s and relegated to
  a stairwell in the Union\, students sought out and ultimately saved this 
 creepy\, but beloved\, piece of history.\n\n \n\nThe exhibition will be on
  view from October 2 - 31. \n\n \n\nOCTOBER EXTENDED HOURS\n\nMonday- CLOS
 ED\n\nTuesday- 11 a.m. - 6 p.m.\n\nWednesday- 11 a.m. - 6 p.m.\n\nThursday
 - 11 a.m. - 9 p.m.\n\nFriday- 11 a.m. - 10 p.m.\n\nSaturday- 11 a.m. - 10 
 p.m.\n\nSunday- 12 p.m. - 6 p.m.
